From: Rob Clark <robin.clark@oss.qualcomm.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 08:09:14 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/a6xx+: Increase GMU FW init timeout

We were using 10ms, kgsl uses 100ms.  In practice it is usually takes
less than 10ms, but very occasionally goes a bit above 10ms, leading to
a "GMU firmware inialization timed out", from which point things go
south.

There are probably some things that could be done to speed up init, like
increasing GMU freq.  But to be safe, increase the timeout to match
kgsl.

Signed-off-by: Rob Clark <robin.clark@oss.qualcomm.com>
Reviewed-by: Konrad Dybcio <konrad.dybcio@oss.qualcomm.com>
Reviewed-by: Akhil P Oommen <akhilpo@oss.qualcomm.com>
Link: https://patch.msgid.link/20260912150915.28700-1-robin.clark@oss.qualcomm.com

[ARMDeck: Nova-Deck kernel/patches/0275 (Armada 0624), fetched with b4
there with both Reviewed-by tags. Our 6.16 a6xx_gmu_start() has the same
10 ms wait. No "GMU firmware initialization timed out" in the last six
boots of the OnePlus 8 (2026-10-29); preventive. Software only: a longer
wait, no clock or voltage change. Test image r18.]
---
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gmu.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gmu.c
index 2a09c5713..d2c44e629 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gmu.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gmu.c
@@ -273,7 +273,7 @@ static int a6xx_gmu_start(struct a6xx_gmu *gmu)
 	gmu_write(gmu, REG_A6XX_GMU_CM3_SYSRESET, 0);
 
 	ret = gmu_poll_timeout(gmu, REG_A6XX_GMU_CM3_FW_INIT_RESULT, val,
-		(val & mask) == reset_val, 100, 10000);
+		(val & mask) == reset_val, 100, 100000);
 
 	if (ret)
 		DRM_DEV_ERROR(gmu->dev, "GMU firmware initialization timed out\n");
